    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp50Tests.coreIdempotentRepeat`.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: `POST /api/owners` carrying an `Idempotency-Key` header should, on a repeat with an already-seen key, return the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which otherwise 409s on the identity check).\n\nI kept everything in the OfficeFloor function-injection style (no controllers), adding a gate at the front of the create pipeline and a record step after save:\n\n**New Spring bean**\n- `rest/support/IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a `@Component` holding an in-memory `key \u2192 ownerId` map, deliberately outside the request transaction so a committed create's key is visible to later requests.\n\n**New pipeline functions** (`rest/function/owner/`)\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 first step. Reads the header off `ServerHttpConnection` (so a missing header is just `null`, not a 400), publishes the key as `Out<String>`, and if the key already maps to a live owner, loads it and fires the `@Flow(\"existing\")` branch \u2014 short-circuiting the rest of the create.\n- `RespondWithExistingOwner` \u2014 the `existing` branch target; takes the owner as `@Parameter` and sends the `OwnerDto` with a default **200**.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 runs after `SaveOwner`/`AuditOwnerCreated` (once the id is assigned); records `key \u2192 id`. No-op when no key was sent.\n\n**YAML wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`)\n- `checkIdempotency` prepended as the entry point with `next: validate` and `outputs: { existing: respondExisting }`.\n- `recordIdempotency` inserted between `audit` and `respond`.\n- Both new create-path branches use `govern: [ transaction ]`, matching the single consistent governance already used across the pipeline.\n\nThe check reads the header rather than binding `@RequestBody`, preserving the \"one `@RequestBody` per pipeline\" rule (still read once, by `ValidateOwnerFields`).",
