    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is every validation and side-effect applied by `POST /api/owners`, in pipeline order.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without it the request is rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header directly off the connection (missing \u2192 `null`, not a 400) and **publishes it** as `Out<String>` for later recording.\n- If the key is present **and** already maps to a stored owner id that still exists and is not soft-deleted \u2192 takes the `existing` branch to `RespondWithExistingOwner`, **skipping the entire create pipeline** (idempotent replay). Otherwise (no key / unseen key / recorded owner gone or deleted) continues to a fresh create.\n\n*(Replay branch `RespondWithExistingOwner`: maps the original owner to a DTO, sets its `bulkSignupWarning` flag, responds **200**.)*\n\n## 2. `ValidateOwnerFields` (the single `@RequestBody` reader)\nValidations (all as 400s):\n- **Address normalization first**: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and flat `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE). Structured lines are preferred when `addressLine1` is non-blank; otherwise the flat `address` is used.\n- **Required-field check** \u2014 rejects if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, address (in either form, checked *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` is blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` with an `errors` array.\n- **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 normalizes to E.164 (assumes +61, drops a leading 0, enforces 8\u201315 digits and country-code-specific national length); unnormalizable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n- **Email** (optional) \u2014 if present, must match the syntactic pattern and must not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException`; stored lower-cased; blank \u2192 `null`.\n\nSide-effects: writes normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address`, E.164 `telephone`, normalized `email` back onto the body, and **republishes the body** as a variable for downstream steps.\n\n## 3. `ValidatePostcode`\n- Postcode optional. If present: must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range; unknown city accepts any 4 digits \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n## 4. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n- If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent date passes.\n\n## 5. `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive). If **\u2265 50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409). (New owner not yet saved, so the 51st is the first rejected.)\n\n## 6. `ResolveRegistrationDate`\n- Side-effect: computes the effective registration date = supplied-or-today, **rolled forward off weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays** to the next business day, and **publishes it** as `Out<LocalDate>`. This one adjusted date drives the daily-limit check, the stored date, and the fiscal-year segment.\n\n## 7. `EnsureDailyCapacity`\n- Counts existing owners whose stored registration date equals that business-day date. If **\u2265 100** \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (429).\n\n## 8. `BuildOwner`\n- Side-effect: maps the validated body to an `Owner` entity and **sets its registration date** to the resolved business-day date. Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n## 9. `AssignHousehold`\n- Side-effect: sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (postcode empty when absent). Mutates the owner in place.\n\n## 10. `EnsureUniqueHousehold`\n- If `sharesHousehold: true` \u2192 bypass. Otherwise, if any non-deleted existing owner has the same `householdId` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n\n## 11. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- If any non-deleted existing owner has the same full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## 12. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- Side-effect only (no rejection). If not a declared household member and postcode is present, finds a non-deleted owner with same last name (case-insensitive) + same postcode + **different** telephone (lowest id wins); if found, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = matchId`. Declared members are never flagged.\n\n## 13. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`\n- Side-effect: sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` **+ 1** (household of one when no `householdId`).\n\n## 14. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- Side-effect: sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode-then-city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`), appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 on collision with an existing code.\n\n## 15. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- Side-effect: sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new owner.\n\n## 16. `SaveOwner`\n- Side-effect: **persists** the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n## 17. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- Side-effect: emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, and derived `membershipNumber`.\n\n## 18. `RecordIdempotencyKey`\n- Side-effect: records `(idempotencyKey \u2192 owner id)` in the `IdempotencyStore` (no-op when no key was sent) so a later repeat replays this owner.\n\n## 19. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Side-effect: maps to `OwnerDto`, sets its `bulkSignupWarning` flag (true when > 80 owners already registered for today's business day), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Transaction note:** every step from `CheckIdempotencyKey` onward carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole create (including the idempotency record) commits once as a single transaction; the three pure-input validators (`ValidateOwnerFields`, `ValidatePostcode`, `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`) are the only steps outside it.\n\nNote also that the entity's `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` bean constraints on `address`, `city`, `telephone` are *not* actively enforced by this pipeline \u2014 validation is done explicitly by the steps above, not via `@Valid`."
